# Authentication & Data Access Model

Authentication is handled by [Clerk](https://clerk.com) via `@clerk/nextjs`, configured in
[layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) (`ClerkProvider`) and [proxy.ts](mdc:src/proxy.ts)
(`clerkMiddleware`, the Next.js 16 replacement for the old `middleware.ts` file).

This is an **internal operational fleet management tool** used by workshop/fleet staff, not a
personal consumer app. Design decisions must reflect that.

## Shared Fleet Visibility — Do NOT Silo Data

- All authenticated staff share access to the same global fleet data. There are no "personal"
  records.
- Never add a `user_id` (or similar ownership) column to `assetsTable`, `mileageLogsTable`, or
  `mechanicalSparesTable` in [schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts) for row-level isolation.
- Never filter, scope, or `WHERE`-clause a query against these tables by the current Clerk
  user/session. Any authenticated user should see and be able to act on the full fleet dataset.
- It's fine to store *who did what* for audit purposes (e.g. a `createdBy`/`updatedBy` field), but
  that must never be used to restrict which rows a user can read.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — silos data per user
const spares = await db.query.mechanicalSparesTable.findMany({
  where: (t, { eq }) => eq(t.userId, userId),
});

// ✅ GOOD — shared visibility across all staff
const spares = await db.query.mechanicalSparesTable.findMany();
```

## Route Protection — Reject Unauthenticated Requests

- Every Next.js App Router page and Server Action that reads or mutates the database must verify
  there is an active Clerk session before touching `db`.
- Use `auth()` from `@clerk/nextjs/server` (or `auth.protect()`) at the top of the page/Server
  Action. Do not rely solely on UI-level checks (e.g. hiding buttons) or on `proxy.ts` alone —
  guard the data access itself.
- On a missing/invalid session, reject strictly: `redirect("/sign-in")` from a page, or `throw`/return
  an error from a Server Action. Never fall through to a DB call for unauthenticated requests.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — Server Action verifies session before mutating
"use server";
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { db } from "@/db";

export async function deleteSpare(id: number) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  return db.delete(mechanicalSparesTable).where(eq(mechanicalSparesTable.id, id));
}
```

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — page verifies session before querying
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { redirect } from "next/navigation";
import { db } from "@/db";

export default async function AssetsPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) redirect("/sign-in");

  const assets = await db.query.assetsTable.findMany();
  // ...
}
```
